\section{Introduction}

Recent deep observations of the neutral hydrogen of several nearby spiral
galaxies  indicate that up to about 15\% of the neutral hydrogen of a
spiral galaxy is located in the halo. The best examples are: 
NGC\,891 \citep{swa97}; 
NGC\,2403 \citep{sch00,fra01}; 
NGC\,4559 \citep{bar05};
M31 \citep{wes05}; 
UGC\,7321 \citep{mat03}; 
NGC\,253 \citep{boo05b};
NGC\,5775 \citep{lee01} and NGC\,6946 \citep{boo05a, boo07}. 
